@startuml
title SysMon - User Creation Sequence Diagram

participant "SysMon Frontend" as Frontend
participant "SysMon Authentication System" as Auth

note over Frontend
  Admin (Tier 1) opens the Users panel, selects Add User,
  enters username, password and tier and commits the changes.
end note

Frontend -> Auth : POST /v1/users\nAuthorization: Bearer token\n{username, password, tier}
Auth -> Auth : Validate token

alt Token missing, invalid or expired
  Auth --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
else Caller is not a Tier 1 admin
  Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
else Data invalid (username, password or tier)
  Auth --> Frontend : 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{code, field, message}
else Username already taken
  Auth --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, message}
else All checks passed
  Auth -> Auth : Create new user account
  Auth -> Auth : Assign selected admin tier
  Auth -> Auth : Initialize account with no permissions
  Auth --> Frontend : 201 Created\nLocation: /v1/users/{userId}\n{userId, username, tier, status, permissions, createdAt}
end

note over Frontend
  After 401, 403, 409 or 422 the Frontend displays the error.
  The admin may correct the form and send the request again.
end note

@enduml
